    fix: handle NaN in regrade_traces.py row parsing
    
    int(row.get("correct", 0)) crashed on hard-kill-corrupted rows with a
    present-but-NaN value. Fixing this and running the tool for the first
    time (50/52 cells, dry-run) shows the previously-circulating "165,000
    labels re-graded, 0.33% flip rate" claim is false, not merely
    unverified: real numbers are approximately 799K rows and a 1.62% flip
    rate -- off by about 4.8x on volume and about 5x in the wrong
    direction on rate.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016jFunoxRUo9oW212ZjYE14

